    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to read this",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Each HITL gate reports the numbers it gates on (`HITL_METRIC` lines, `pi/hitl/harness/hitl_metrics.py`; older gates are parsed from the lines they already print). The ingest (`pi/hitl/observability/metrics/`) pulls them out of every `hitl.yaml` run's job log every 3 h.\n\n**Headroom** = limit / p50 and limit / p95 (for a floor, p50 / limit). Near 1 = the gate flakes. Above **3\u00d7 p50 or 2\u00d7 p95** the limit is so loose that a real regression can pass: watch the **drift** column (p50 of the last 7 days vs the 30 days before) instead. Audit: `docs/hitl/gate-thresholds.md`.\n\n**Lane**: `main` = pushes, merge queue and scheduled runs on main; `pr` = PR branches. Points are coloured by rig; the red dashed line is the gate's limit, the grey lines its p50 / p95 over the last 90 days."
      }
    },
